# One rule: TOOL settings go in .env.local (copy this file there), COMPOSE settings go in .env. Both files are yours and untracked.
#   .env.local  is read by the tools (tts, align, render ...); compose hands it to the media container as its environment.
#   .env        is read by Docker Compose itself to fill ${...} in compose.yaml (image names, your user id, voice server knobs).
#               A compose setting put in .env.local is ignored. Needs Docker Compose v2.24 or newer (`docker compose version`).
# Create .env once (Linux: run as you, so files the container writes are yours):
#   printf 'HOST_UID=%s\nHOST_GID=%s\n' "$(id -u)" "$(id -g)" > .env
#
# ---- .env.local (tool settings) ----
# fixture: no voice, silent audio sized from the example's committed timeline.json (offline first run, see examples/ep01-kettle/README.md)
# http: a voice server (compose profiles below, default URL); ssh: a voice server inside a container on another machine
VOICE_TRANSPORT=fixture
VOICE_URL=http://voice:8080
# The name of a preset voice on the server (http/ssh without cloning). Not needed for fixture or for cloning.
VOICE_NAME=
# Sent with every request; servers that have no steps (Chatterbox, Kokoro) ignore it.
VOICE_NUM_STEP=24
# How long tts waits for a voice server whose /health says ready:false (the first Chatterbox start downloads about 3.19 GB): seconds.
# VOICE_READY_WAIT=1800
# Overrides the engine name tts puts in its cache key (normally the server's /health reports it; needed after changing VOICE_IMAGE).
# VOICE_ENGINE_TAG=
# ssh transport only:
# VOICE_SSH_HOST=
# VOICE_CONTAINER=
# Optional render host over ssh:
# RENDER_HOST=
# RENDER_DIR=ai-creator
#
# SEO research (tools/seo.js, docs/seo.md). A free API key from your Google Cloud project, for the top-video lookup; without it, suggestions only.
# YOUTUBE_API_KEY=
# Daily budgets the SEO tool refuses to exceed (Pacific-time days): shared-pool units (shared with uploads), and search.list calls.
# SEO_QUOTA_BUDGET=800
# SEO_SEARCH_BUDGET=50
#
# Cloning YOUR OWN voice (recommended lane: Chatterbox, `docker compose --profile chatterbox up -d voice-chatterbox`, or chatterbox-cpu).
# tts refuses to clone until voice/CONSENT.md exists and is filled in (copy voice/CONSENT.example.md).
# VOICE_REF=voice/ref.wav
# VOICE_REF_TEXT=the exact words spoken in the recording
#
# Other lanes, each answers as http://voice:8080 (VOICE_URL unchanged); run one voice profile at a time:
#   --profile cpu-clone up -d voice-cpu-clone   OmniVoice on CPU, cloning; CC-BY-NC weights (non-commercial), optional
#   --profile gpu up -d voice                   OmniVoice on an NVIDIA GPU; same licence
#   --profile cpu up -d voice-cpu               Kokoro presets, no cloning (VOICE_NAME=af_heart; list: GET /v1/voices)
#
# ---- .env (compose settings; put these lines in .env, not here) ----
# HOST_UID=1000
# HOST_GID=1000
# Chatterbox settings "F" (read by the voice server at start, and passed to the media container so the tts cache sees a change;
# restart the voice service after changing them): exaggeration, cfg_weight, temperature; seed unset = random (a set seed makes
# every retake the same, so besttake and fixaudio cannot help).
# VOICE_EXAGGERATION=0.6
# VOICE_CFG_WEIGHT=0.3
# VOICE_TEMPERATURE=0.9
# VOICE_SEED=
# Pace and pauses (applied by the tts stage, any voice engine). The clone follows the pace of your reference clip; VOICE_TEMPO slows
# or speeds the speech without changing pitch (0.9 = ten percent slower, 0.5 to 2). Each sentence is synthesized on its own and joined
# with real silence: VOICE_PAUSE_SENTENCE after . ! ? and VOICE_PAUSE_PARAGRAPH at a blank line, in seconds, as heard after the tempo
# change (0 for both = leave it to the voice model). Changing any of these re-makes every cached take once.
# Audio8 lane (compose profile audio8; set in .env): sampling temperature (0.8), plus VOICE_REF_TEXT in .env.local, which Audio8 requires.
# AUDIO8_TEMPERATURE=0.8
# VOICE_TEMPO=0.9
# VOICE_PAUSE_SENTENCE=0.4
# VOICE_PAUSE_PARAGRAPH=0.8
# CHATTERBOX_TORCH_INDEX=https://download.pytorch.org/whl/cu124
# VOICE_IMAGE=            (override the OmniVoice GPU image)
# EPISODE=examples/ep01-kettle   (the episode `--profile preview up preview` serves)
